    <node id="Rajjo Gujjar   Discord Bot">
      <data key="d0">Rajjo Gujjar   Discord Bot</data>
      <data key="d1">Organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Rajjo Gujjar   Discord Bot is a sophisticated integration of modern AI capabilities with traditional Discord bot functionality, providing both entertainment and utility value for Discord communities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e3e568634fa88961bff7dd56df3bb43</data>
      <data key="d4">pdf_82e6ce95.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1758307701</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Discord">
      <data key="d0">Discord</data>
      <data key="d1">Platform</data>
      <data key="d2">Discord is the platform where the Rajjo Gujjar   Discord Bot operates.&lt;SEP&gt;Discord is a social platform for communities to communicate and interact through text, voice, and video chat.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-75601805fceec3389a50199b8f98ad50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e3e568634fa88961bff7dd56df3bb43</data>
      <data key="d4">pdf_82e6ce95.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1758307701</data>
    </node>
    <node id="API Security">
      <data key="d0">API Security</data>
      <data key="d1">Concept</data>
      <data key="d2">API Security refers to measures taken to prevent unauthorized access and attacks on APIs.&lt;SEP&gt;API security is crucial for preventing unauthorized access and attacks on APIs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e3e568634fa88961bff7dd56df3bb43</data>
      <data key="d4">pdf_82e6ce95.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1758307701</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Rate Limiting">
      <data key="d0">Rate Limiting</data>
      <data key="d1">Method</data>
      <data key="d2">Rate limiting is a method used to prevent abuse by limiting the number of requests that can be made within a certain time frame.&lt;SEP&gt;Rate limiting can help prevent abuse by limiting the number of requests that can be made within a certain time frame.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e3e568634fa88961bff7dd56df3bb43</data>
      <data key="d4">pdf_82e6ce95.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1758307701</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Error Handling">
      <data key="d0">Error Handling</data>
      <data key="d1">Method</data>
      <data key="d2">Error handling refers to strategies for dealing with errors and exceptions in code, including preventing information disclosure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e3e568634fa88961bff7dd56df3bb43</data>
      <data key="d4">pdf_82e6ce95.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1758307701</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Input Validation">
      <data key="d0">Input Validation</data>
      <data key="d1">Method</data>
      <data key="d2">Input validation is the process of checking user input to prevent attacks such as SQL injection and cross-site scripting (XSS).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e3e568634fa88961bff7dd56df3bb43</data>
      <data key="d4">pdf_82e6ce95.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1758307701</data>
    </node>
    <node id="Message Content Sanitization">
      <data key="d0">Message Content Sanitization</data>
      <data key="d1">Method</data>
      <data key="d2">Message content sanitization involves removing or escaping special characters in messages to prevent XSS attacks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5e3e568634fa88961bff7dd56df3bb43</data>
      <data key="d4">pdf_82e6ce95.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1758307701</data>
    </node>
    <node id="File Type Verification">
      <data key="d0">File Type Verification</data>
      <data key="d1">Method</data>
      <data key="d2">File type verification is a method used to ensure that uploaded files are of the expected type and size.</data>
